WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.130 --> 00:00:06.130
United Overseas Bank Bhd is collaborating
with Prudential Assurance Malaysia Berhad

00:00:06.130 --> 00:00:10.280
to provide customers with a suite of insurance
solutions digitally through a new virtual

00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:15.170
face-to-face feature on Pulse1, the insurer’s
all-in-one health and wellness app.

00:00:15.170 --> 00:00:21.519
It said UOB Malaysia was the first bank in
Southeast Asia to use the VF2F feature, enabling

00:00:21.519 --> 00:00:26.179
its customers to manage their insurance needs
digitally and conveniently, particularly important

00:00:26.179 --> 00:00:27.779
during the ongoing pandemic.

00:00:27.779 --> 00:00:33.290
“The VF2F feature also enables the bank’s
customers to submit the necessary documentation

00:00:33.290 --> 00:00:37.710
and forms electronically, eliminating the
need to fill in a physical questionnaire.

00:00:37.710 --> 00:00:42.820
“As the entire process, from receiving financial
guidance to applying for and confirming their

00:00:42.820 --> 00:00:47.080
insurance coverage is conducted on the app,
customers can fulfil their protection and

00:00:47.080 --> 00:00:51.420
wealth planning needs in a simpler, smarter
and swifter manner without visiting a branch,”

00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:53.130
it said in a joint statement.

00:00:53.130 --> 00:00:57.910
UOB Malaysia managing director and country
head of personal financial services Ronnie

00:00:57.910 --> 00:01:02.870
Lim said the collaboration with PAMB demonstrated
the bank’s commitment to providing customers

00:01:02.870 --> 00:01:06.329
with progressive and convenient solutions
that are relevant to their lifestyle needs

00:01:06.329 --> 00:01:08.619
and preferences and in the manner they prefer.

00:01:08.619 --> 00:01:13.649
“The introduction of the VF2F feature to
offer customers protection solutions is timely

00:01:13.649 --> 00:01:16.590
given the latest surge in Covid-19 cases.

00:01:16.590 --> 00:01:21.329
“With more consumers using smartphones to
manage their financial needs, we hope that

00:01:21.329 --> 00:01:25.490
one in every two customers will benefit from
this new feature and sign up for the protection

00:01:25.490 --> 00:01:29.729
or wealth solutions that we offer together
with PAMB,” Lim said.

00:01:29.729 --> 00:01:35.389
PAMB senior director, partnerships distribution
Lee Ee Hui said the pandemic had elevated

00:01:35.389 --> 00:01:39.520
the awareness of insurance protection and
the critical need to be financially protected.

00:01:39.520 --> 00:01:44.630
“With this partnership, we are able to offer
UOB Malaysia’s customers a secure end to-end

00:01:44.630 --> 00:01:54.780
service anytime, anywhere through our AI-powered
health app, Pulse,” he said.

